course: dictionary
lesson: 5078
title: Insulation: keeping heat in or out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insulation is a material that stops heat, cold, sound or electricity from passing through easily. You can work out its meaning from the words around it. «Thick walls, fluffy loft insulation and double windows slow heat leaking out of a house, so it needs much less fuel to keep warm.» The clues are slow, leaking, much less fuel and keep warm, so insulation must be something that stops heat getting out.
explain: Insulation works in both directions. «Insulation slows heat flow in both directions, so a coat wrapped round a snowman makes it last longer.» The coat slows the warm air from getting in, so the snowman melts more slowly. The same idea keeps a snowman cold, so a coat is a kind of insulation.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The same flask keeps tea hot and juice cold all day.» If we swap in "a material that slows heat moving in or out", the sentence still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Insulation is a material that slows heat, cold, sound or electricity from passing through.
fact: Wool, foam, feathers, fur and air are good thermal insulators, so they keep heat in or out.
fact: Plastic and rubber are electrical insulators; they cover wires so that we do not get shocks.
fact: Homes have loft and wall insulation to save energy and keep warm.
fact: Insulation is uncountable, so we say «some insulation», not «two insulations».
exercise: «Thick walls, fluffy loft insulation and double windows slow heat leaking out of a house.» What does insulation do in this sentence? | It turns heat into light | It makes heat leak out faster | *It slows heat from leaking out | It makes the house louder
exercise: Which material is a good thermal insulator? | *Feathers | Copper | Steel | Iron
exercise: Which material covers wires to stop us getting electric shocks? | Copper | Steel | *Rubber | Silver
test: «A flask keeps tea hot and juice cold all day.» What is the job of the flask's insulation? | Making the drink louder | *Slowing heat from moving in or out | Adding colour to the drink | Stopping the drink being poured
test: Which phrase means insulation that stops sound passing through? | Thermal insulation | *Sound insulation | Wire insulation | Loft insulation
exam: «Real house mice build nests out of shredded paper, cloth, insulation and fluff.» What does the insulation do in a mouse nest? | *It slows heat escaping, helping keep the nest warm | It makes the nest fit through a gap as wide as a pencil | It makes a noise that scares predators | It is food that the mice eat later
